{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh will not hearken to you.</b> Not before the hardening, nor even afterward when he sees the multitude of signs and wonders. Therefore I will execute judgments upon them — namely, the plague of the firstborn and the drowning of Egypt in the Sea of Reeds — these two alone being punitive, measure for measure. But the rest of the plagues were signs and wonders to bring them to repentance, as it says: בְּזֹאת תֵּדַע כִּי אֲנִי ה'; <b>בַּעֲבוּר תֵּדַע כִּי אֲנִי ה' בְּקֶרֶב הָאָרֶץ</b> (Exodus 8:18); <b>לְמַעַן תֵּדַע כִּי לַה' הָאָרֶץ</b> (Exodus 9:29); <b>לְמַעַן שִׁיתִי אֹתֹתַי אֵלֶּה בְּקִרְבּוֹ</b> (Exodus 10:1); <b>וּלְמַעַן תְּסַפֵּר וִידַעְתֶּם</b> (Exodus 10:2) — both you, Israel, and the Egyptians. And even when He drowned them in the sea, His intent was to act in such a manner that those remaining in Egypt would recognize and know, as it says: <b>וְיָדְעוּ מִצְרַיִם כִּי אֲנִי ה'</b> (Exodus 14:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:43.616425233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}